# Every secret and metered key this deployment needs, in one file.
#
#   cp devnet/.env.example devnet/.env && chmod 600 devnet/.env
#   $EDITOR devnet/.env
#
# `devnet/.env` is gitignored, this file is not, so never put a live value here.
#
# It sits outside `devnet/.state/`, which `teeism teardown` deletes. Nothing you type here is
# lost to a teardown.
#
# A setting in the process environment overrides this file (`FOO=x teeism ...`).
#
# Two readers, so the syntax is the intersection of both: `KEY=value`, `#` comments, quotes
# around anything containing a space, and no `export`.
#   - `teeism` reads it for every command.
#   - `teeism-relayer.service` names it as its EnvironmentFile.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- required

# Pays for every relayer submission on the EVM chains, and signs deployments and owner
# transactions unless EVM_SIGNER=ledger (below). Needs gas on every EVM chain in use.
#
# Keep the `0x`. teeism accepts it either way, but systemd hands this to the relayer
# verbatim and does no normalising of its own.
EVM_PRIVATE_KEY=0x

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- optional

# Sign EVM deployments and owner transactions on a Ledger instead of with EVM_PRIVATE_KEY:
# the Ledger then owns every contract, and EVM_PRIVATE_KEY only relays. Ethereum app open,
# blind signing on. EVM_LEDGER_PATH picks an account other than the first. Needs teeism built
# with `--features ledger`.
# EVM_SIGNER=ledger
# EVM_LEDGER_PATH=m/44'/60'/0'/0/0

# The 24 words the chain's genesis accounts derive from, and the phrase to import into Keplr:
# account 0 is the funded one.
#
# Leave it empty and `teeism celestia up` generates one and writes it back into `devnet/.env`. Keeping
# it means the address a wallet already imported still holds funds after the chain is rebuilt;
# losing it means every genesis mints fresh keys and that wallet goes empty.
CELESTIA_MNEMONIC=

# Sepolia's execution endpoint for the relayer, which must serve `eth_getProof` at finalized
# blocks. Default: the host's reth at http://127.0.0.1:8545 (DEPLOY step 6b). Never a metered
# key: the dispatch index sweeps `eth_getLogs` through it too. teeism sends Sepolia
# transactions through SEPOLIA_SEND_RPC, else this, else the public endpoint.
SEPOLIA_RPC=

# The Alchemy key for the Base and Arbitrum archives, the one metered endpoint this deployment
# needs. Each route reads the tree at its ISM's trusted height, which can be days old, and no
# free endpoint serves `eth_getProof` that far back. A free tier is enough: it is read once per
# ISM advance.
#
# `teeism config` puts it in the `rpc` of `[chains.base]` and `[chains.arbitrum]` and nowhere
# else; logs and reads near the head go to the public endpoints. ALCHEMY_BASE_KEY, the older
# name, still works. Set BASE_ARCHIVE or ARBITRUM_ARCHIVE to a full url to use another provider.
ALCHEMY_KEY=

# Slack. With both set, the relayer posts every problem as it opens and resolves, and a status
# post every SLACK_EVERY_SECS (default 1800), so a silent channel means the relayer has stopped.
# The bot token needs chat:write, and the bot must be in the channel. EXPLORER_URL makes each
# problem a link to its page on the explorer.
SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=
SLACK_CHANNEL=
#SLACK_EVERY_SECS=1800
#EXPLORER_URL=http://<host>:3001

# `teeism upstream check` (daily, from teeism-upstream.timer): OpenAI judges each new release
# of what we depend on against deploy/upstream.toml. Only public text is sent: release notes and
# the manifest, never anything from this file. Breaking and maybe items go to the dashboard and
# to the Slack channel above. GITHUB_TOKEN (read-only, no scopes) raises GitHub's limit of 60
# requests an hour.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
#OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-5
#GITHUB_TOKEN=
